      "problem": "If $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-1,$ then $(f∘f)(x)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we note that $(f∘f)(x)$ is equivalent to $f(f(x)).$\n\nTo find $f(f(x)),$ we write down the function $f$ and replace every occurrence of $x$ with $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =2{x}^{2}-1 \\\\ f(f(x)) & =2(f(x))^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $f(x)=2{x}^{2}-1$ into the right-hand side of the above and simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(f(x)) & =2(f(x))^{2}-1 \\\\  & =2(2{x}^{2}-1)^{2}-1 \\\\  & =2(4{x}^{4}-4{x}^{2}+1)-1 \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $(f∘f)(x)=8{x}^{4}-8{x}^{2}+1.$",
